                    <p>
                        Version 1.6 · Documentation updated October 21, 2026 · Ergotron FULL sandbox
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Marketing_Submission__c preserves a submission snapshot separately from the Lead or Contact and the work generated for Sales. Capture uses the original incoming CRM ID first and email only when that ID is blank. Downstream processing classifies the submission from that original ID, assigns eligible Tasks to a queue, and creates one enhanced Note related to the person and, when present, the Task.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Latest requested capture change:</strong> when neither Contact nor Lead is found, still execute Create Marketing Submission with blank person lookups. Capture V7 is now active and its saved canvas includes that change. V6 previously discarded unmatched submissions. This documentation update did not modify or activate Flows.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Release scope:</strong> sandbox documentation only. Capture V6 and Task and Note Follow Up V2 were activated and tested October 21; the user&#x27;s subsequent Capture V7 no-match change is now active and its saved connector was inspected. A V7 runtime test was not performed during this documentation update. The legacy processor is inactive. No production deployment, action mapping change, permission change, or live Marketing App Extension test is part of this release. The October 14 production V3/B2BMA results below are historical evidence, not validation of the new design. This sandbox has no Marketing App Extensions.
                    </p>
