                    <p>
                        This self-contained Visualforce guide uses inline HTML and CSS. It has no Apex controller, Static Resource, JavaScript library, or CRM operations. Flows execute the solution; this page documents it. Solution attribution: DemandChain · Brandon Walton.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="architecture-and-record-ownership">
                        Architecture and record ownership
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        One Marketing Submission represents one captured invocation or identified source event. Separate submissions from the same person remain separate snapshots. A genuine source event key can suppress a retry of that event.
                    </p>
                    <div class="pipeline" aria-label="Submission processing architecture">
                        <div>
                            MCAE External Action
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            Original CRM ID; blank-ID email fallback
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            V7: capture even when no person matches
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            Async person resolution; pending if unresolved
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            Existing: queue Task + Note linked to person and Task
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            New: person Note only
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="caption">
                        Active V7 retains unmatched submissions; its saved path is verified, with runtime testing still pending. Both identity inputs blank still ends normally. Follow Up V2 creates outputs only after resolving a CRM person. Sandbox evidence and historical production tests are distinguished below.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The diagram includes the active V7 change: identity present but no person match still reaches capture. Both identity inputs blank still ends normally. V7 activation was verified in Flow Builder; its no-match execution still needs a focused runtime test.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Capture owns the original values and initial lookup result. The processor owns processing status, Task outcomes and Note links. The Task represents Sales work. The Note records readable submission context. Neither Flow creates a Lead or Contact. The conversion-linking Flow can maintain later relationships; it does not supply an automatic pending-submission retry service.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="crm-first-matching-and-unmatched-submission-capture">
                        CRM-first matching and unmatched submission capture
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        The original trimmed <code>crmRecordId</code> selects the matching strategy. Email is used only when that original input is blank; a supplied ID never redirects to another person through email.
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-wrap">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Input / lookup result
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Capture behavior in active V7
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Follow-up behavior
                                    </th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        CRM ID matches a Contact
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Store original ID and Contact lookup
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Existing: queue Task and person Note; same Note also linked to Task
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        CRM ID matches a Lead
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Store original ID and Lead lookup, even when email matches a different Contact
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Existing: queue Task and Note; converted Lead activity resolves to its converted Contact
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        CRM ID blank; email matches Contact
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Contact-first fallback; original CRM ID stays blank
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        New: person Note only, even though the Contact already exists
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        CRM ID blank; no Contact, email matches unconverted Lead
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Store Lead lookup; original CRM ID stays blank
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        New: person Note only
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        Identity supplied; no Contact or Lead found
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Create Marketing Submission still executes</strong>, with blank person lookups and Received status; existing-key skip still applies
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Unresolved person: Pending CRM Match; no Task or Note can be related yet
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        Both CRM ID and email blank / whitespace
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Blank Identity - End before person queries or creation
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        No submission or downstream work
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>
                        <strong>V7 change and saved labels:</strong> both Lead Found outcomes now merge into Create Marketing Submission. The old default label <code>No Match - End</code> and some resource descriptions still describe earlier behavior; the saved connector determines execution. V7 now shows Active in Flow Builder. Its connection supersedes V6&#x27;s quiet no-match exit. No V7 runtime test is claimed here.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Duplicate email selection:</strong> Contact takes precedence over Lead. Current fallback queries use LastModifiedDate descending and keep the first matching record, inherited from Capture V5. This supersedes the older guide&#x27;s CreatedDate-ascending/oldest-record description. There is no secondary tie breaker for equal timestamps. Email is not unique and this selection does not prove the chosen record is canonical.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        A Contact match sets <code>Contact__c</code>; otherwise a Lead match sets <code>Lead__c</code>. Internal match variables clear when no record is returned. Email fallback excludes converted Leads; an explicit Lead ID may resolve a converted Lead for downstream Contact linkage. <code>CRM_Record_ID__c</code> stores <code>TRIM({&#33;crmRecordId})</code>, never an email-resolved ID.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The capture ID-shape guard accepts 15/18-character Contact (<code>003</code>) or Lead (<code>00Q</code>) identifiers for lookup; it is not checksum validation. A malformed supplied ID still blocks email fallback. With V7, its no-match branch can reach insertion; field limits, query and DML faults still apply. In particular, original IDs longer than the field&#x27;s 18-character limit cannot be captured unchanged. Invalid IDs can also require correction before downstream ID queries can succeed. Do not describe invalid input as guaranteed successful processing.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        An unmatched V7 submission preserves the supplied details for reconciliation. A later connector sync does not automatically rematch it: the processor uses captured CRM ID/lookups, and no scheduled email-rematching service was added. Link a verified person under a controlled reconciliation procedure, preserve the original ID classification, and retry only after inspecting prior outcomes.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="capture-and-mcae-input-contract">
                        Capture and MCAE input contract
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        All ten existing inputs remain Text and retain their API names. After identity lookup, capture resolves generic versus legacy asset names, chooses the supplied event key or interview GUID, converts optional source time, and writes Received. V7 also reaches this step without a matched person. An existing Submission Key skips creation without overwriting the original. Tasks and Notes remain downstream.
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-wrap">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Flow input
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        MCAE value or configuration
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Destination / rule
                                    </th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>assetName</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Descriptive literal configured for the asset
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>Asset_Name__c</code>, max 255; used for Task subject and Note title
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>assetKey</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Stable literal such as business-unit:asset-type:asset-id
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Existing <code>Form_Key__c</code>, max 255
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>submittedEmail</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>{{Recipient.Email}}</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Trim for fallback matching; retain supplied value in <code>Submitted_Email__c</code>, max 254. ID-only capture is supported.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>crmRecordId</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>{{Recipient.ID}}</code> or a verified source-preserved CRM ID
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Original Salesforce Lead/Contact ID, 15/18 characters. Trim into <code>CRM_Record_ID__c</code>; supplied = Existing, blank = New. Never populate it from a later email match.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>submissionDetails</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Readable context and supported prospect merge fields
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>Submission_Details__c</code>, object limit 32768; Task Description limit is 32000
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>prospectId</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Verified numeric MCAE prospect ID, otherwise blank
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>Prospect_ID__c</code>, max 80; do not map Recipient.ID here
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>submissionKey</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Genuine unique source event key, otherwise blank
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>Submission_Key__c</code>, max 255; reuse only for a retry of the same event
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>submittedAtUtc</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Validated original UTC timestamp, otherwise blank
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>Submitted_At__c</code>; format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>formName</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Legacy callers
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Fallback only when assetName is blank
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>formKey</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Legacy callers
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Fallback only when assetKey is blank
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>
                        Salesforce documents <code>{{Recipient.ID}}</code> as the prospect&#x27;s Lead or Contact CRM ID. It is not the numeric MCAE prospect ID. HML resolves when the action executes; a prospect that acquires a CRM ID before that moment may therefore be classified Existing. If the requirement is an immutable form-submit-time distinction, provide a source-preserved original-ID value rather than assuming HML proves historical existence. <apex:outputLink value="https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.pardot_handlebars_merge_fields.htm&amp;language=en_US&amp;type=5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Salesforce HML reference</apex:outputLink>.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Asset identity is not event identity. Never use assetKey, email, or person ID alone as Submission Key, because legitimate repeat submissions would be suppressed. A blank key produces an interview GUID, which distinguishes invocations but does not identify external retries. Blank source time stays null; CreatedDate is Salesforce capture time. Validate optional timestamps upstream: invalid date text previously converted to null in testing.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Submission Details is the text the action supplied. It is not an automatic raw form POST or a guaranteed event-time answer snapshot. Keep it within 32000 characters when the Existing branch must also populate a Task. Current mappings do not silently truncate oversized content; object/Task errors require correction. Verify MCAE action-control limits separately.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="field-dictionary-submission-identity-and-source-facts">
                        Field dictionary — submission identity and source facts
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        These eight fields store source facts, including the original incoming CRM identifier. Resolved identities belong in Contact and Lead. The two legacy asset aliases preserve caller compatibility without adding object fields. Field types below are Salesforce storage types, which can differ from the Flow input type.
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-wrap">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Field and API name
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Type / input
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Purpose and design guidance
                                    </th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Submission Key</strong> — <code>Submission_Key__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(255), unique case-insensitive, External ID; <code>submissionKey</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Identity of one source event. Reuse the same value for retries; use a different value for each genuine submission. Proposed convention: source + business unit + source event ID. Do not use email, prospect ID, or form key alone. Case-only differences are duplicates. Indexed.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Form Key</strong> — <code>Form_Key__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(255); <code>assetKey</code>, legacy <code>formKey</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Stable asset identifier for routing and reporting. The existing field retains its original label/API name. Qualify by business unit and asset type; keep it stable when the display name changes. Currently not indexed.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Asset Name</strong> — <code>Asset_Name__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(255); <code>assetName</code>, legacy <code>formName</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Human-readable configured asset name captured with the event. Supports assets beyond forms and form handlers. Keep as a snapshot; use Asset Key for stable routing.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Prospect ID</strong> — <code>Prospect_ID__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(80); <code>prospectId</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Source Account Engagement prospect identifier for support and reconciliation. It is not a Salesforce record ID or relationship. Proposed: pair with business unit identity before cross-unit matching.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>CRM Record ID</strong> — <code>CRM_Record_ID__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(18); <code>originalCrmId = TRIM({&#33;crmRecordId})</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        V6/V7 preserve the original input. Supplied = Existing; blank = New. Do not backfill from a later email match or use it as the resolved-person field. Historical V3 records stored an email-resolved ID and cannot safely be reclassified using this rule without migration review.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Submitted Email</strong> — <code>Submitted_Email__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(254); <code>submittedEmail</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Original email supplied at action execution, retained if the person&#x27;s current email later changes. Capture trims a separate value for fallback matching. This is Text, not Salesforce Email type; email alone is not unique.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Submitted At</strong> — <code>Submitted_At__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Date/Time; <code>submittedAtUtc</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Verified source event time, when available. Input convention is UTC <code>YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS</code>. Blank remains null; malformed date text can also become null. Do not substitute Salesforce intake time and call it source time.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Submission Details</strong> — <code>Submission_Details__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Long Text Area(32768); <code>submissionDetails</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Preserved supplied context and merge values for Sales or later processing. Does not automatically receive the original HTTP payload, parse JSON, or make arbitrary keys reportable. Promote fields needed for filtering or routing into typed fields.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Current replay behavior:</strong> capture trims a supplied key and skips an existing record with that key without overwriting answers. If no key is supplied, it uses the Flow interview GUID. That fallback identifies an invocation, not a source event, and cannot recognize retries. Concurrent inserts can still cause a duplicate-key fault even though the unique constraint prevents duplicate records.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Source fidelity matters:</strong> a merge field populated from the latest prospect profile is not necessarily a snapshot of a particular submission. Validate available source values during production integration testing, including two rapid consecutive submissions. Do not require event metadata that the source cannot supply.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="field-dictionary-relationships-and-processing">
                        Field dictionary — relationships and processing
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        These five custom fields support relationships and downstream processing. Capture initializes available matched lookups and Processing Status Received; the processor owns later status, message, and Task outcomes. Do not expose these fields as marketer-controlled External Action inputs.
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-wrap">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Field and API name
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Type
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Purpose and design guidance
                                    </th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Lead</strong> — <code>Lead__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Lookup(Lead), indexed
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Capture populates the ID-matched Lead, or an unconverted email match when original ID is blank and no Contact matches. Retain after conversion to preserve provenance; it may later coexist with Contact.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Contact</strong> — <code>Contact__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Lookup(Contact), indexed
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Capture populates the ID-matched Contact or Contact-first email fallback; a supplied Lead ID is never overridden by email. The conversion Flow can later fill an empty Contact link while retaining Lead. A relationship does not itself grant access to the person record.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Processing Status</strong> — <code>Processing_Status__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(80)
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Current lifecycle: Received, Pending CRM Match, Routed, Processed, or Error. Routed is intermediate; Processed confirms required Note links completed. Historical Failed values belong to the old processor. V7 no-match creates Received for downstream reconciliation; fully blank identity still creates nothing.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Processing_Message</strong> — <code>Processing_Message__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(255)
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Short operator explanation; completion includes New/Existing classification, Note ID and optional Task ID. No dedicated Note ID field was added. Actual label contains an underscore. Keep longer diagnostics in logs.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Follow Up Task ID</strong> — <code>Follow_Up_Task_ID__c</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Text(18)
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        ID of the created Task and a guard against normal reprocessing. It is not a lookup, does not enforce that the Task still exists, and is not a concurrency lock. Do not clear it to force another run. For multiple actions per submission, use proposed child execution records instead of adding an ID field for each action.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>
                        Interpret CRM Record ID by capture version: original input in V1/V2 and V6/V7; email-resolved in V3; the inspected V5 Create Records did not map it. Do not blindly requeue historical records under the new classification. For a New pending submission, link the verified person through Contact/Lead and leave the original CRM ID blank. Corrections to a supplied original ID require an explicit audit and classification review.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="field-dictionary-standard-fields">
                        Field dictionary — standard fields
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        These five standard fields complete the 18 fields shown in Fields &amp; Relationships.
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-wrap">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Field and API name
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Type
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Purpose and design guidance
                                    </th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Submission Number</strong> — <code>Name</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Auto Number, indexed
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Human-friendly reference for support, related lists, and Task context. Recorded format is <code>MS-{00000000}</code>. It is assigned after creation and is not a source replay key.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Owner</strong> — <code>OwnerId</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Lookup(User,Group), indexed
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Ownership of the submission record for access and operational responsibility. This is separate from Task ownership. Queue support for Tasks does not establish queue support for this object.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Created By</strong> — <code>CreatedById</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Lookup(User)
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Salesforce actor that created the record. Helpful for integration auditing; it does not identify the human who submitted the form.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Last Modified By</strong> — <code>LastModifiedById</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Lookup(User)
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Actor responsible for the most recent update, including automation. It does not supply a complete change history.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <strong>Currency</strong> — <code>CurrencyIsoCode</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Picklist
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Record currency in this multicurrency org. No custom monetary field is present, so it currently provides no submission-value or revenue-attribution calculation.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>
                        Useful system fields beyond this visible field list include <code>Id</code> for record links and relationships, <code>CreatedDate</code> for Salesforce intake time, and <code>LastModifiedDate</code> for the latest update. LastModifiedDate is not a substitute for an explicit processing-completion timestamp.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The October 1 handoff recorded reports, search, and history enabled; individual tracked fields and broader access were unfinished. Object-level history enablement alone does not mean every field is tracked. Activities were disabled, so current Tasks relate to the person through WhoId rather than using this object as WhatId.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="production-marketing-app-extension-setup">
                        Production Marketing App Extension setup
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Historical verified production registration, October 13, 2026:</strong> extension Salesforce Integration (<code>SalesforceIntegration</code>), action Marketing Submission (<code>Marketing_Submission</code>), invocable action <code>Marketing_Submission_Capture</code>, business unit IUS Ergotron (149221). Both the extension and action were Active in Automations at that verification. The successful execution used B2BMA Integration. The sandbox has no extension registration.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <apex:outputLink value="https://ergotron.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/MarketingAppExtAction/2YoiM000000JDhVSAW/view" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Production action and schema</apex:outputLink> · <apex:outputLink value="https://ergotron.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/0mFiM0000000001UAA/view" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Production extension</apex:outputLink> · <apex:outputLink value="https://ergotron.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/FlowRecord/2aFiM0000011lE1UAI/view" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Production capture Flow</apex:outputLink>.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Salesforce supports Flow Builder invocable actions for External Actions. Select the active autolaunched capture Flow, retain generated Parameters and default Required entries, and keep the <code>properties</code>, <code>view</code>, and <code>required</code> schema sections. All capture inputs use strings. The observed Parameters are <code>{&quot;isStandard&quot;:false,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;flow&quot;}</code>; do not change generated Parameters to configure field visibility. <apex:outputLink value="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/marketing/pardot/guide/external-actions-guide.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Salesforce External Actions guide</apex:outputLink>.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Configure the form or form handler&#x27;s <strong>Execute External Action</strong> completion action to call this intake action. External Action completion actions support both forms and form handlers. <apex:outputLink value="https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.mcae_execute_external_actions_using_completion_actions.htm&amp;language=en_US&amp;type=5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Salesforce completion-action guidance</apex:outputLink>.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        In a new org, deploy the object and active Flow, create the extension/action, associate the correct business unit, and configure B2BMA permissions before testing an Execute External Action completion action. A direct administrator Flow debug run does not prove the integration user&#x27;s access.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="visible-fields-and-marketing-app-extension-crmrecordid-mapping">
                        Visible fields and Marketing App Extension crmRecordId mapping
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        The Flow&#x27;s Available for Input checkbox does not make a parameter visible or populate it. Configure the External Action schema and the saved form/form-handler action. The new CRM-first contract uses the same Flow API/input names, but changes the meaning of <code>crmRecordId</code> compared with V3.
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-wrap">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Input
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Recommended configuration
                                    </th>
                                    <th scope="col">
                                        Visible to marketers?
                                    </th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>assetName</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Actual descriptive asset name; required for Task/Note title
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Yes
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>assetKey</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Stable business-unit/asset identifier
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Yes
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>submissionDetails</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Approved readable submission context and supported HML
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Yes, optional
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>submittedEmail</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Default <code>{{Recipient.Email}}</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Normally hidden
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>crmRecordId</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Default <code>{{Recipient.ID}}</code>, or verified original source CRM ID
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Normally hidden; optional value so an unsynced prospect can be New
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>prospectId</code>, <code>submissionKey</code>, <code>submittedAtUtc</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Blank unless verified source metadata exists
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Normally hidden and optional
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        <code>formName</code>, <code>formKey</code>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Keep existing caller compatibility during migration
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        Avoid for new configurations
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>
                        <strong>CRM mapping fragment:</strong> merge this property into the action&#x27;s existing <code>properties</code> object. This is not a replacement schema. Retain <code>properties</code>, <code>view</code>, and <code>required</code>, generated required fields, other mappings and generated Parameters. Leave crmRecordId out of <code>view.components</code> when it should be an automatic hidden value.
                    </p>
                    <pre><code>&quot;crmRecordId&quot;: {
                    &quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;,
                    &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Original Salesforce CRM Record ID&quot;,
                    &quot;value&quot;: &quot;{{Recipient.ID}}&quot;
                    }</code></pre>
                    <p>
                        To expose it for an administrator-reviewed configuration, add the following component to the existing view. A visible default is editable, so arbitrary marketer IDs can change both the person and Task eligibility. Hidden mapping is the recommended operational setup.
                    </p>
                    <pre><code>{
                    &quot;definition&quot;: &quot;lightning/control&quot;,
                    &quot;scope&quot;: &quot;#/properties/crmRecordId&quot;
                    }</code></pre>
                    <p>
                        The property&#x27;s title sets its label; value supplies its default; view.components controls visibility. Schema configuration does not grant object/field permissions. Reopen and review saved completion actions after a schema change; a new default alone does not prove an existing action supplies it. <apex:outputLink value="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/marketing/pardot/guide/external-actions-guide.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Salesforce External Actions schema guidance</apex:outputLink>.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Mapping acceptance:</strong> trace the actual invocation and verify raw crmRecordId, trimmed CRM Record ID, resolved Contact/Lead, and final processing result. A mapped existing Contact/Lead must receive a Task plus Note. A genuinely blank original ID with a matched person must receive only a Note. A supplied ID conflicting with email must retain ID priority. Confirm the active V7 no-match capture path and no automatic person creation. Do not place <code>{{Recipient.OwnerId}}</code> or the numeric prospect ID in crmRecordId.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Historical production schema, October 14:</strong> visible controls were only assetName and formName. submittedEmail defaulted to <code>{{Recipient.Email}}</code>; crmRecordId defaulted to empty and was hidden. Four properties existed and required was empty. Six other Flow inputs were absent. That schema successfully called V3, which ignored the CRM hint. It does not prove CRM-ID mapping for V6/V7. If reused unchanged with the new processor, blank IDs classify matched submissions as New and suppress Tasks. No production action schema was changed in this sandbox documentation release.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Completion actions are unordered. HML reflects the value available at execution, so do not assume another completion action has already assigned/synced the prospect or frozen an earlier CRM ID. Keep original identity, source timing and classification expectations explicit. <apex:outputLink value="https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.pardot_completion_actions_considerations.htm&amp;language=en_US&amp;type=5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Completion-action considerations</apex:outputLink>.
                    </p>
