                    <p>
                        <strong>Repeat-form testing:</strong> duplicate activity rows can be condensed even when completion actions run, so check prospect Audits. The tested form had Always Display Form disabled and could show the existing thank-you content on a return visit. Use a fresh private session or the documented <code>?PI_ALWAYS_DISPLAY=1</code> test parameter and actually submit the form. If an activity is missing, inspect the form&#x27;s Tools → Show Filtered Activities; filtered activity can suppress completion actions. A later refresh during the successful test revealed the new 2:54 PM submission, followed by Flow execution at 2:55:28 PM. <apex:outputLink value="https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=mktg.pardot_forms_testing.htm&amp;language=en_US&amp;type=5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Salesforce form testing guidance</apex:outputLink> · <apex:outputLink value="https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=000383485&amp;language=en_US&amp;type=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Form troubleshooting</apex:outputLink>.
