                    <h2 id="fault-handling-and-known-follow-up-work">
                        Fault handling and known follow-up work
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        Both-blank identity still ends normally. Active V7 no-match now attempts capture and is not a fault by itself. Real lookup/insert errors remain visible. In Follow Up V2, handled queue/Task failures mark Error; unhandled Note or Note-link failures roll back the asynchronous transaction while the separate capture record remains committed. Inspect failed interviews and logs before retrying; do not treat an intermediate Routed state as completed processing.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The earlier production failure reached Create_Marketing_Submission&#x27;s fault connector. Its Send_Email action then failed because B2BMA could not use the organization-wide sender sales@ergotron.com. That secondary error was returned to MCAE and obscured the original create error; the handled create error&#x27;s exact message was not printed in that trace. No delivered fault email did not mean the Flow never ran.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Recommended diagnostic improvement: capture <code>{&#33;$Flow.FaultMessage}</code> into a Text variable immediately on the Create Records fault path, then include that saved error, <code>{&#33;$Flow.InterviewGuid}</code>, Flow name, timestamp, and asset key in the diagnostic email. Use a verified organization-wide sender that the running user is permitted to use. Check Setup → Organization-Wide Addresses and test the fault branch under the integration identity. Avoid unnecessary personal data in notifications. Give the notification action its own fault handling so a sender error does not become the only available diagnostic.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The existing static email body did not include the create error. Correcting the sender and improving the error body remain follow-up work; the successful capture did not exercise or validate that branch. If creation fails, no Marketing Submission record exists to hold Processing_Message__c, so do not rely on that field as the only capture-error log. This page documents the changes to make; it does not implement them.
                    </p>
