                    <h2 id="new-versus-existing-and-processing-lifecycle">
                        New versus Existing and processing lifecycle
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        The active processor is Marketing Submission - Task and Note Follow Up V2 (<code>Marketing_Submission_Contact_Follow_Up</code>). It is an after-save, created-or-updated Flow with an asynchronous path. It runs when a record newly meets Processing Status Received and Follow Up Task ID blank. Normal edits to Processed records do not reprocess them. The old Marketing_Submission_Process is inactive and must remain inactive while this processor is enabled.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Classification is based on the original submission, not CRM CreatedDate:</strong> a nonblank original CRM Record ID means Existing; blank means New. Email fallback must never backfill this field. A New submission can resolve to an existing Contact or Lead and still gets no Task. New does not mean this solution created a Lead; it never creates people.
                    </p>
