                    <p>
                        Processing Message records New/Existing, Note ID, and optional Task ID. Follow Up Task ID stores the Task ID; it is Text, not a lookup or concurrency lock. A New Processed record legitimately has a blank Task ID. Never reset completed records blindly: New records have no Task-ID guard against manually re-entering Received and creating another Note.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        For a pending New record with no outcomes, set the verified Contact/Lead lookup while leaving original CRM ID blank, then move Pending CRM Match back to Received. A record already meeting start conditions may need a controlled transition before it requalifies. Reconcile invalid supplied IDs with an audit trail; do not quietly turn Existing into New. Reusing an event key only skips capture; it does not update the pending record or rematch it.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="task-queue-assignment-and-field-mappings">
