                    <p>
                        Both Note links use ShareType Viewer (<code>V</code>) and Visibility InternalUsers. The Note&#x27;s Related to list shows the person and Task where both apply. This is one shared Note with two links, not duplicate Note records. A Task is related to its person through WhoId; the Note links are additional relationships. Verify appropriate Notes related lists/page presentation for the intended Sales users.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The processor escapes ampersands and angle brackets, then converts actual line feeds into HTML paragraphs before setting ContentNote.Content. This preserves literal values such as <code>A&amp;B</code> and <code>&lt;test&gt;</code> plus multiline formatting. Submitted text is not treated as executable markup. Note-only and Task-linked rendering were verified in sandbox. <apex:outputLink value="https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=004693703&amp;language=en_US&amp;type=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Salesforce ContentNote line-break behavior</apex:outputLink>.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Without a resolved person, the processor cannot create these relationships. The active V7 capture change preserves the Marketing Submission for reconciliation; it does not create an orphan Note or a Lead automatically.
                    </p>
                    <h2 id="extending-the-design-without-one-apex-class-per-use-case">
                        Extending the design without one Apex class per use case
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        Keep capture stable and add behavior behind the saved submission. Proposed examples include Campaign Member updates, Case creation, Sales Tasks, or supported declarative integration actions. These are extension patterns, not current implemented outcomes.
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-wrap">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
