                    <h2 id="deployment-and-rollback">
                        Deployment and rollback
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        This release updates only the existing sandbox documentation page. The preceding October 21 sandbox rollout activated Capture V6 and Follow Up V2 and deactivated Marketing_Submission_Process. The user subsequently saved and activated Capture V7 to retain no-match submissions; Active status and the saved connector were verified before publication. Production guide and automation were not changed.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        For promotion, retrieve and review the approved live object/fields, capture and follow-up Flows, retained conversion-linking Flow, Task queue, intended access and page layouts. The local documentation manifest contains only page/tab metadata and cannot deploy the automation. Use developer-name queue lookup rather than a sandbox ID. Disable overlapping processors before enabling follow-up traffic.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Coordinate capture and processor versions: CRM_Record_ID__c changed meaning across versions. Historical V3 stores email-resolved identity; V6/V7 store the original incoming ID. Do not run historical submissions through New/Existing logic without reviewing that distinction. Keep original input untouched during blank-ID reconciliation. Review existing saved action mappings even though Flow API names remain stable.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        For rollback, review existing Tasks/Notes and the capture contract before activating an earlier approved version. V7 → V6 restores no-match discard; earlier versions can change CRM-ID meaning and duplicate selection. Never enable the old processor alongside the current one. A documentation rollback restores the archived pre-v1.6 sandbox source/description only and does not roll back Flows or business records. Production remains outside this guide update.
                    </p>
